Z||000000||Gerald||11-02-2001||02:47 PM||||Ok so I know Im kicking a dead dog here but what I got from the archives was a lot opinion and very little fact. I have decided on a camshaft (260H grind) and I will be getting the metal timing gears. I know the stock crank leaves alot to be desired and I want to replace that. I will not be trying to get a SD block. I want the holly tb but the car is an 87 so it will need to be adapted to my intake. The intake will be ported but not polished. Im gonna get the head ported and polished. Or I might get the SD head. New rods and pistions will not be stock and everything will be balanced. Im getting the MSD DIS2 ignition. What kind of numbers can I hope for with this setup. And please dont tell me to swap in a v6 or a v8. I also will not get a Quad 4 for obivios reasons. By the way right now the car will hit nearly 200 kph on a stright flat stretch of highway.<P>Sorry about the length of the post. Any comments short of a swap are welcomed.<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||11-02-2001||03:00 PM||||Not sure if you said you want to replace the crank or not.<BR>If so, it will be difficult. The DIS uses a timing wheel that is part of the crank.<BR>Good luck with your project.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||MR2KLR||11-02-2001||11:00 PM||||I'm Glad to hear someone wants to build a Duke right. I will try to find you a link to a company I think names "Kansass racing products" they make custom cranks & rods they will also balance your rods & crank they also sell compleete SD4's The only way I see to get around the weak crank id to Retro-fit a older Duke that does not use a DIS igniton system. this will alow you to use stroker cranks and alow you to use a Holley Intake as well as a Holley TBI. also don't use hyper pistons. A APEXI S-AFC can work with our cars MAP sensor as far as I know to help control & boost the fuel curve.  When you have the head & intake ported don't forget the exhaust manifold. use NOS like a 50-70 shot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I was going to build a high HP duke but then got rid of he car, Now my next project is on the way but it has a DIS duke (88 Coupe) and I will be installing a 3.4L W/ a Carb I hope Gook luck to you & your Duke<P>Tips:<BR>#1 Don't use Hyperwhatc-a-mcallit pistons<BR>#2 Don't even think about a turbo<BR>#3 NOS is OK becaues it won't stress the engine 100% o the time<BR>#4 The stock headgasket is VERY weak under NOS or Turbo use<BR>#5 Turbo dukes eat more head gaskets than Quad-4's in death valley<BR>and #6 there was a 2.7/3.0L duke marine motor produced (but I never found any info on it) The crank & block may work||||reg||1
Z||000003||blazin'||11-02-2001||11:08 PM||||I'm personally still debating on either swapping to a 2.8 that is balanced and blueprinted with a few mods thrown in or getting the ol' duke rebuilt much like you said! But this is one of the many things on my mind regarding my fiero at this time..<p>[This message has been edited by blazin' (edited 11-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||aleroboy||12-12-2001||06:44 PM||||I have a 86 2.5 that is freshly rebuilt with about 8k mi on the new motor.<BR>It was in my old car till the car got totaled.<BR>The engine has port work, aluminum roller rockers, roller cam (regrind from comp cams,)<BR>chrme molly pushrods, larger stainless steel valves, the block has been deck 050 to give it true 9.6:1 compression it has 030 over badger pistons and has been completely rebalenced. if anyone is interested in this engine please drop me a line at johnbelveal@hotmail.com||||reg||1
